## Description

In .NET 9 MAUI, modal pages no longer trigger MainActivity `OnKeyDown` and other key event overrides on Android. This is a regression from .NET 8 MAUI where these overrides worked correctly even when modal pages were displayed.

### Root Cause

Modal pages in .NET 9 use `ComponentDialog` which intercepts all key events before they can reach the main activity. The current system only forwards `OnBackPressed` events through the AndroidLifecycle system, but other key events are consumed by the modal dialog.

### Solution

This PR extends the existing AndroidLifecycle event pattern to include key events, ensuring MainActivity overrides are called regardless of whether modal pages are open.

## Changes Made

### 1. Added new AndroidLifecycle events
```csharp
public delegate bool OnKeyDown(Activity activity, Keycode keyCode, KeyEvent? keyEvent);
public delegate bool OnKeyUp(Activity activity, Keycode keyCode, KeyEvent? keyEvent);
public delegate bool OnKeyLongPress(Activity activity, Keycode keyCode, KeyEvent? keyEvent);
public delegate bool OnKeyMultiple(Activity activity, Keycode keyCode, int repeatCount, KeyEvent? keyEvent);
```

### 2. Enhanced MauiAppCompatActivity
Added key event overrides that invoke lifecycle events:
```csharp
public override bool OnKeyDown(Keycode keyCode, KeyEvent? e)
{
    var preventKeyPropagation = false;
    IPlatformApplication.Current?.Services?.InvokeLifecycleEvents<AndroidLifecycle.OnKeyDown>(del =>
    {
        preventKeyPropagation = del(this, keyCode, e) || preventKeyPropagation;
    });

    if (!preventKeyPropagation)
        return base.OnKeyDown(keyCode, e);

    return true;
}
```

### 3. Updated CustomComponentDialog
Modified the modal dialog to forward key events to the main activity through lifecycle events, similar to how `OnBackPressed` is already handled.

## Testing

### Before (Broken)
```csharp
public class MainActivity : MauiAppCompatActivity
{
    public override bool OnKeyDown(Keycode keyCode, KeyEvent? e)
    {
        // This was NOT called when modal pages were open
        Debug.WriteLine($"Key pressed: {keyCode}");
        return base.OnKeyDown(keyCode, e);
    }
}
```

### After (Fixed)
```csharp
public class MainActivity : MauiAppCompatActivity
{
    public override bool OnKeyDown(Keycode keyCode, KeyEvent? e)
    {
        // This IS now called even when modal pages are open
        Debug.WriteLine($"Key pressed: {keyCode}");
        return base.OnKeyDown(keyCode, e);
    }
}
```

## Verification Steps

1. Connect an external keyboard to an Android device/emulator
2. Override `OnKeyDown` in MainActivity with logging
3. Open a modal page using `Navigation.PushModalAsync()`
4. Press keys on the external keyboard
5. Verify that MainActivity.OnKeyDown is called and logged

This restores the .NET 8 MAUI behavior where MainActivity key event overrides work consistently regardless of modal page state.

